_startup.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_artwork_lifecycle.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_config.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_dimensions.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_settings.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_surface_parity.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_unattended.py", "tests/preferences/test_example_env_locks_nothing.py", "tests/preferences/test_screen_tables.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/accessibility-spec.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/agents-and-memory.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-unattended-settings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/information-architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/museum-label-findings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md", ".prawduct/changes/unattended-settings.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "Settings > General shows unattended spend only in two of its five states, and never the remaining figure", "recommendation": "Chunk 03 says the section shows 'what it has spent this month against the allowance', and the verification strategy says to 'see the allowance's remaining figure fall'. general.js renders only `unattended.sentence`. That sentence carries $spent of $allowance only in the may-run and allowance-spent branches of UnattendedAllowance.standing. When the switch is off, there is no key, or the allowance is $0.00, the screen shows no spend at all, so a household that switched work off mid-month cannot see what it already spent. `remaining_usd` and `spent_usd` come back from GET /api/unattended but the client never reads them, so the planned verification step cannot be carried out. Scope: instance. Either render spent/allowance/remaining from the route's fields beside the sentence, and add a browser assertion over a seeded unattended spend row, or record the narrowing explicitly in the plan and the IA row, which currently says only 'whether such work may start now, or why not'.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/general.js", "arrt/tests/browser/test_general_settings.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "test_switching_it_on_with_an_allowance_says_it_may_run asserts the no-key refusal, so the may-run screen path is untested in the browser", "recommendation": "The test's name promises the screen says unattended work may run. Its final assertion is the opposite: 'There is no model key, so unattended work has nothing to spend with.' The browser suite therefore never shows the may-run sentence (or any $spent of $allowance figure) on the page. Integration's TestWithAModelKey covers the route only. Per the core learning 'When you drop or rewrite a test's assertion ... re-read the test's name against it', either give this test a key (override the `key_status` fixture, as TestWithAModelKey does) and assert the may-run sentence, or rename it to what it checks and add a keyed case. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/tests/browser/test_general_settings.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "MCP surface value has no length bound while the route caps it at 200", "recommendation": "SetSetting.value is Field(max_length=200), but art_settings(action='set') passes `value` to SettingsService.set unbounded, and `_MODEL_ID` has no length limit. So an agent can store an arbitrarily long unattended_model that the browser could not have sent, and the two surfaces refuse different inputs. Scope: instance. Put the bound in the service (for example in `Setting.checked` or `_model`) so both surfaces share it, and drop or keep the route's cap as a second guard.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/settings.py", "arrt/src/arrt/http/models.py", "arrt/src/arrt/mcp/bindings.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "rule-unenforced: tool tallies copied into prose; the MCP server's INSTRUCTIONS still say 'Five tools' with seven registered", "recommendation": "Two written rules already cover this. The core learning says 'When a claim already lives in prose, verify it against the code and add a pointer, never a copy'. tools.py's docstring and api-contract.md record the lesson that tool tallies drift ('the tally was a copy'). Yet arrt/src/arrt/mcp/server.py INSTRUCTIONS, which every MCP client is sent, opens 'Five tools'. It was stale from art_taste on, and this change adds art_settings, making seven. No check owns it: no test reads INSTRUCTIONS against TOOLS. Today nothing depends on the number, since clients get the real tool list. To mechanize it, assert in the contract suite that INSTRUCTIONS states no tool count, or that any count it states equals len(TOOLS). Also drop the number from the sentence. Scope: class. Search MCP-facing strings, including descriptions and tips, for spelled-out tool counts.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/mcp/server.py", "arrt/src/arrt/mcp/tools.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "The General screen places the unattended standing line by a hard-coded setting key, while its header says the server owns the settings' layout", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. general.js `section()` decides where `/api/unattended`'s sentence goes with `members.some((setting) => setting.key === \"unattended_work\")`, and EMPTY_WORDS is keyed by `unattended_model`. That means the client knows the server's setting keys, even though the module comment says the settings, sections and labels are the server's and \"only the words for a choice's values are written here\". The browser test asserts the standing line, so renaming the key would fail loudly, not silently. Leave the code as it is, or when Watches next touches this screen, key the placement on the section name the server sends (`UNATTENDED_SECTION`), or have `/api/unattended` name its section. If you keep it, make the header comment relational rather than exclusive. No edit is wanted in this commit.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/general.js"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "A $0.00 allowance and a spent allowance share one Refusal value", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `UnattendedAllowance.standing()` returns `Refusal.ALLOWANCE_SPENT` both for `allowance == 0` and for a spent allowance. Only `sentence` tells them apart, and `refusal` is the machine-readable field the route and the `art_settings(action='unattended')` tool expose (`allowance_spent`). Nothing calls `may_start` yet (the plan defers that to Watches), so nothing goes wrong today. When the Watches scheduler or an agent starts branching on `refusal`, consider a distinct `NO_ALLOWANCE` value so a caller can say \"choose an allowance\" rather than \"spent\". Otherwise accept.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/unattended.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "scope-trace: two unattended controls have no reader, and the screen's sentence reads as if work runs", "recommendation": "Instance. The plan records the gap as an accepted tradeoff with a revisit trigger ('The allowance check, the cadence and the model have no caller until the Watches plan'). Nothing in arrt/src reads UNATTENDED_CADENCE or UNATTENDED_MODEL, and nothing calls UnattendedAllowance.standing except GET /api/unattended and art_settings(action='unattended'). The household is the one misled. On Settings \u203a General, 'How often' and 'Model' accept and store a value that changes nothing. Once Unattended work is on with an allowance, the server's standing sentence reads 'Unattended work may run: $X of this month's $Y is spent.' Neither the screen nor the setting descriptions say what the change record says: 'nothing yet runs unattended either way'. A household that switches it on and sets an hourly cadence will expect standing work and see none. The cheapest fix is a server-owned clause in the may-run sentence or the section saying nothing starts unattended work yet, which a browser test can pin. Accepting the finding under the recorded tradeoff is also legitimate.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/unattended.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/settings.py", "arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/general.js"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner, and two alignment-pass misses", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Listed so the owner can read them in one place. Settled by convention or rule: POST rather than PUT ('this surface writes with POST everywhere'); the table in SqliteDiscovery (seam rules); a change logged, not written to history_events (that table's subject); a label from the server for each setting ('One word per thing'); an empty model meaning the discovery model ('do it right'); on/off as a choice (one control per kind); a stored value held to today's rules when read ('fails closed'); one UTC-month function. Still the builder's inference: General placed after Sources and before Taste; cadence as hourly/daily/weekly rather than an interval. Alignment-pass misses, recorded in the plan as such: removing LABEL_UNITS from .env.example ('The goals did not foresee this'), and GET /api/unattended plus art_settings(action='unattended'), which the plan needed and did not name. Priors: R-9 (rev-20261109T185523Z-60216a34, accepted) covers the defaults and what cadence means, which remain inferred, so it is not re-raised here. Precedence has since been ruled (be8aff18).", "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: no finding rests on a regressed rule", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Read core.md, surface.md and tooling.md, the list `learnings-files --for-diff` prints. 'When you delete a constant or add a required parameter, grep `tools/` and `scripts/` for consumers': DEFAULT_LABEL_UNITS, Settings.label_units and the label_units parameter of Services.bind are gone, and grep finds no remaining consumer in arrt/tools, scripts or the suites. The change conforms. No learnings file changed this cycle, so the new-rule pass has nothing to rate. No rule-unenforced case: the rule that .env.example must lock nothing is held by tests/preferences/test_example_env_locks_nothing.py.", "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog reconciliation: nothing resolved, and the cache does not hold #329", "recommendation": "Scope: none. `cache-query affecting` over all 47 changed files returned 0 items. The cache was 6h old. #417 (a stored value failing its check shows as default, with a log line on every read) was filed this cycle and stays open. It covers the Goal 6 concern about _state's fallback, so that concern is not raised here. C-B4: `resolve 329` reports 'no item in the cache claims that id', though .prawduct/changes/unattended-settings.md has `closes: [brookstalley/arrt#329]`. #329 was probably closed already, or is outside the open set the cache holds. Check its state before the merge, so the closes: line does not name an issue that someone closed before the work shipped.", "fid": "R-10"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 3, "note": 7}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 480, "scope": "unattended-settings", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "abdceccec5d22f011126225085cecd35b63e4bb8", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/accessibility-spec.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/agents-and-memory.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-unattended-settings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/information-architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/museum-label-findings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md", ".prawduct/changes/unattended-settings.md"], "c