ly survives outside the MCP-facing string, and no check holds INSTRUCTIONS against a count", "recommendation": "Class. R-4 named tool tallies copied into prose. The MCP-facing site is fixed: server.py INSTRUCTIONS now states no count, and a search of src/arrt/mcp and http/static for spelled-out counts finds only two hits. One is tools.py:11, a history note that is correct. The other is arrt/src/arrt/mcp/__init__.py:4, whose module docstring still reads 'tools.py declares the five tools', with seven registered. No client is sent it. The optional contract-suite assertion was not added. Accept by default, or make the docstring relational ('declares the tools') in a commit already happening.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261109T201520Z-09a792ab", "fid": "R-4"}, "oid": "O-2"}], "duration_seconds": 240, "scope": "unattended-settings", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-09T20:23:43Z"}}
